            "output": "<path>/workspace/build-python.sh</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: #!/bin/sh\n2: \n3: # [description]\n4: #\n5: #     Prepare a source distribution (sdist) or built distribution (wheel)\n6: #     of the Python package, and optionally install it.\n7: #\n8: # [usage]\n9: #\n10: #     # build sdist and put it in dist/\n11: #     sh ./build-python.sh sdist\n12: #\n13: #     # build wheel and put it in dist/\n14: #     sh ./build-python.sh bdist_wheel [OPTIONS]\n15: #\n16: #     # compile lib_lightgbm and install the Python package wrapping it\n17: #     sh ./build-python.sh install [OPTIONS]\n18: #\n19: #     # install the Python package using a pre-compiled lib_lightgbm\n20: #     # (assumes lib_lightgbm.{dll,so} is located at the root of the repo)\n21: #     sh ./build-python.sh install --precompile\n22: #\n23: # [options]\n24: #\n25: #     --boost-dir=FILEPATH\n26: #                                   Directory with Boost package configuration file.\n27: #     --boost-include-dir=FILEPATH\n28: #                                   Directory containing Boost headers.\n29: #     --boost-librarydir=FILEPATH\n30: #                                   Preferred Boost library directory.\n31: #     --boost-root=FILEPATH\n32: #                                   Boost preferred installation prefix.\n33: #     --opencl-include-dir=FILEPATH\n34: #                                   OpenCL include directory.\n35: #     --opencl-library=FILEPATH\n36: #                                   Path to OpenCL library.\n37: #     --bit32\n38: #                                   Compile 32-bit version.\n39: #     --cuda\n40: #                                   Compile CUDA version.\n41: #     --gpu\n42: #                                   Compile GPU version.\n43: #     --hdfs\n44: #                                   Compile HDFS version.\n45: #     --integrated-opencl\n46: #                                   Compile integrated OpenCL version.\n47: #     --mingw\n48: